{"name":"Canvas Luggage","hex":"#e2d7c6","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"canvas","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A type of coarse cloth, woven from hemp (traditionally) or from cotton and polyesters, useful for making sails, tents, and overcoats or as a surface for paintings.","A piece of such cloth stretched across a frame on which one may paint an artwork."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To cover (an area or object) with canvas."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/canvas"},{"term":"luggage","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The bags and other containers that hold a traveller's belongings.","The contents of such containers."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/luggage"}],"entries":[{"title":"Canvas","blocks":[{"text":"Canvas is a durable plain-woven fabric used for making sails, tents, marquees, backpacks, shelters, as a support for oil painting and for other items for which sturdiness is required, as well as in such fashion objects as handbags, electronic device cases, and shoes. It is popularly used by artists as a painting surface, typically stretched across a wooden frame."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/94/Sj%C3%B6manss%C3%A4ck_-_1991.jpg/330px-Sj%C3%B6manss%C3%A4ck_-_1991.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Canvas","wikidata":"Q4259259"},{"title":"Baggage","blocks":[{"text":"Baggage, or luggage, consists of bags, cases, and containers which hold a traveler's personal articles while the traveler is in transit. A modern traveler can be expected to have packages containing clothing, toiletries, small possessions, and trip necessities. On the return trip, travelers may have souvenirs and gifts. For some people, baggage and the style thereof is representative of the owner's wealth and status."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/53/20180520_Away_carryon_%281%29.jpg/330px-20180520_Away_carryon_%281%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Baggage","wikidata":"Q865054"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2a/MetroBrussel_Erasmus.jpg/500px-MetroBrussel_Erasmus.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2a/MetroBrussel_Erasmus.jpg/500px-MetroBrussel_Erasmus.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Canvas roof at the Erasmus station of the Brussels Metro","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMetroBrussel_Erasmus.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/02/Bitwa_pod_Grunwaldem_Muzeum_Narodowe_05.JPG/500px-Bitwa_pod_Grunwaldem_Muzeum_Narodowe_05.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/02/Bitwa_pod_Grunwaldem_Muzeum_Narodowe_05.JPG/1280px-Bitwa_pod_Grunwaldem_Muzeum_Narodowe_05.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/02/Bitwa_pod_Grunwaldem_Muzeum_Narodowe_05.JPG/500px-Bitwa_pod_Grunwaldem_Muzeum_Narodowe_05.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"One of Poland's biggest canvas paintings, the Battle of Grunwald, 1878, by Jan Matejko (426 cm × 987 cm (168 in × 389 in)), displayed in the National Museum in Warsaw[1]","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABitwa_pod_Grunwaldem_Muzeum_Narodowe_05.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/db/Splined_Canvas.jpg/330px-Splined_Canvas.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/db/Splined_Canvas.jpg/330px-Splined_Canvas.jpg?utm_source=en.w